  "answer": "### Issue Presented\nUnder Philippine tax law, an overseas contract worker (OCW) or overseas Filipino worker (OFW) is required to file a Philippine income tax return only for income derived from sources within the Philippines. This is governed by Section 24 of the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC), which states that an individual citizen of the Philippines who is working abroad is taxable only on income derived from sources within the Philippines.\n\nSpecifically, Section 24(A)(1)(b) of the NIRC provides that an individual citizen of the Philippines residing outside the country, including OCWs, is subject to income tax on income derived from sources within the Philippines. Therefore, if the OCW's income is solely from foreign sources, they are not required to file a return for that income in the Philippines. \n\nIn summary, OCWs must file a return only if they have income sourced from the Philippines.",
